// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 5b. Board certification tasks: the non-CME duties each board sets, as dated
// recurring tasks (src/utils/boardTasks.js). Keyed "<AOA|ABMS>:<board code>";
// an AOA discipline (AOA-SUB:AOBS:Neurological Surgery) uses its parent
// board's list. Only cadences an official page states are here; every other
// board keeps its `assessment` sentence.
//   every:  "year" (calendar year); { years: 3, anchor: "aoaCycle" } (the
//           fixed AOA cycle, 2025-2027, ...; `due` "MM-DD" sets the day in
//           its last year, Dec 31 otherwise); { years: N, anchor:
//           "certExpiration" } (a cycle that ends on the certificate's
//           expiration date: due that date, or `due` "MM-DD" in the
//           expiration year plus `dueYearOffset`); or { years: N } (a
//           cycle the app cannot date: no due date, `dueRule` says it)
//   due:    "MM-DD" each year (`opens` "MM-DD" when the board states it), or
//           windows: { YYYY: { from, to } } for a published year; a year
//           with neither has no dated deadline
//   dueRule: the board's own rule in a few words, shown when no date can be
//           computed from it; never alerted
//   disciplines: true when an AOA discipline card shares these steps (AOBS)
//   startsYearOfExpiration: the board starts the task in the year a
//           certificate on the old exam track expires: one issued in or
//           before oldExamTrackIssuedThrough, the track whose assessment
//           starts in the expiration year. Later certificates are
//           time-limited too (the portal says so of a 2025 one); what sets
//           the tracks apart is when the assessment starts, not whether the
//           certificate expires
//   oldExamTrackIssuedThrough: the last issue year on that old track; a
//           later certificate starts the task at once, whatever date it shows
//   validThru: the AOA "valid thru" date. Every AOA certificate on the
//           current track shows one in the AOA Physician Portal: the end of
//           the current OCC cycle, moved forward as the steps are met
//           (portal, read 2026-11-18). It is the certificate's date like any
//           other; the card explains it and asks for it when none is on file.
//   whereToCheck: { label, url } where a diplomate sees each step's status
//   contact: who to ask, only when an official page states it
//   sources: the pages the set was checked against (`checked`)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
